## Component Composition Pattern

### Creating Variant-Specific Components

When creating preset variants (Display, Title, Label, etc.), use simple wrapper pattern:

**✅ Recommended Pattern:**

```typescript
// Base type for all variants
type TextBaseProps = {
  as?: React.ElementType
  size?: TextSize
  children?: React.ReactNode
  className?: string
  style?: React.CSSProperties
  ref?: React.Ref<any>
}

// Variant components - no forwardRef needed
const Display = (props: TextBaseProps) => {
  return <Text variant="display" {...props} />
}

const Title = (props: TextBaseProps) => {
  return <Text variant="title" {...props} />
}
```

**Why no forwardRef?**

- Base `Text` component already handles ref forwarding
- Wrapper just passes props through
- Simpler, less boilerplate
- ref support is automatic

**Benefits:**

- Explicit API: Only expose props you want
- Type control: Prevent prop overload from `Pick`/`Omit`
- Simple: No complex type gymnastics
- ref works: Automatically forwarded to base component

